@startuml
'https://plantuml.com/class-diagram
!theme spacelab

title Device Contract — Intent-Driven API

interface Device {
  +open(): CompletableFuture<Response<Void>>
  +read(query: DeviceQuery): CompletableFuture<Response<DeviceState>>
  +execute(command: DeviceCommand): CompletableFuture<Response<Void>>
  +close(): void
}
note right of Device
  The ONLY API an application author sees.
  No protocol vocabulary, no CommunicationClient,
  no PointAddress — just intent in, Response out.
end note

interface DeviceQuery
note right of DeviceQuery
  Command pattern (read side): encapsulates a read
  request as an object. The device maps the query to
  the required protocol operations. Examples for MVHR:
  ReadSnapshot, ReadTemperatures, ReadAirQuality,
  ReadAlarms. A snapshot is explicit, not an accidental
  consequence of calling read without parameters.
end note

interface DeviceCommand
note right of DeviceCommand
  Command pattern (write side): encapsulates a
  requested operation as a stand-alone object.
  Commands are device-specific and are translated
  by the device into protocol-level writes.
  Examples for MVHR: SetPower, SetFanSpeed,
  SetTemperature, ResetFilterTimer.
end note

class Response<T> {
  +status: Status
  +details: String
  +value: T
}

Device ..> DeviceCommand : accepts
Device ..> DeviceQuery : accepts
Device ..> Response : returns

note as N1
  How Device implementations are created and
  supplied is covered in 05 Device Plugin Factory.
  Concrete devices (MVHR, relay, analog output)
  are shown in 06 Example Device Extensions.
end note

@enduml
